WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:22.400
Hannah and the Hurricane by John Escott. Penguin readers, easy start.

00:22.500 --> 00:26.100
Hannah is 16 and lives on an island. 

00:26.200 --> 00:33.300
She is on holiday from school and is working for Mr. Duval on his glass-bottomed boat.

00:33.400 --> 00:38.950
They take people to look at the beautiful fish and the coral reef under the sea.

00:39.000 --> 00:46.400
Mr. Duval can only pay Hannah a little money, but she likes working for the old man.

00:46.500 --> 00:52.200
Mr. Duval's boat is the only glass-bottomed boat on the island.

00:52.300 --> 00:56.950
But one day...

00:57.000 --> 00:59.800
Look Mr. Duval, says Hannah. 

01:00.000 --> 01:02.950
There's a new glass-bottomed boat.

01:03.000 --> 01:04.900
Hannah is right. 

01:05.000 --> 01:09.050
The new boat is taking people out to look at the coral reef

01:09.100 --> 01:12.950
and there are people waiting for it to come back.

01:13.000 --> 01:19.950
Why are all the people going on the new boat and not on my boat? Says Mr. Duval.
 
01:20.000 --> 01:21.950
What's happening?

01:22.000 --> 01:25.600
I'm going to find out, says Hannah.

01:25.700 --> 01:35.400
Hannah soon has the answer. 

01:35.500 --> 01:37.950
It's cheaper, she says.

01:38.000 --> 01:41.950
Yes, says a man standing behind her.

01:42.000 --> 01:48.950
And it's going to be the only glass-bottomed boat on the island in a month or two.

01:49.000 --> 01:53.950
It's going to be goodbye, Mr. Duval.

01:54.000 --> 01:58.100
And he laughs. Hannah knows the man. 

01:58.200 --> 02:00.950
His name is Max Marker.

02:01.000 --> 02:05.950
He is very rich and has a big house on the island.

02:06.000 --> 02:08.950
Is it your boat? She asks.
 
02:09.000 --> 02:12.950
Yes, he says.

02:13.000 --> 02:16.950
Why is it cheaper on your boat? Hannah asks.

02:17.000 --> 02:20.400
Oh, I know, she says.

02:20.500 --> 02:26.950
You want to stop Mr. Duval's boat and then your prices can go up.

02:27.000 --> 02:28.950
Max smiles.

02:29.000 --> 02:32.200
Come and work for me, he says. 

02:32.300 --> 02:35.500
I can pay you lots of money.

02:35.600 --> 02:37.950
No, says Hannah.

02:38.000 --> 02:41.000
I like working for Mr. Duval. 

02:41.100 --> 02:43.400
Money isn't everything.

02:43.500 --> 02:46.600
You're wrong, says Max. 

02:46.700 --> 02:56.600
He's laughing again, but it is not a nice laugh.

02:56.700 --> 02:58.700
The weeks go by. 

02:58.800 --> 03:02.950
People do not come to Mr. Duval's boat.

03:03.000 --> 03:11.200
I'm sorry, but there is no more work for you, Hannah, says Mr. Duval one day.

03:11.300 --> 03:18.100
It's okay, says Hannah, but she is very sad to lose her job.

03:18.200 --> 03:21.950
Max goes to see the old man.

03:22.000 --> 03:26.500
Do you want to sell your boat? He asks.

03:26.600 --> 03:29.950
I can give you a good price for it.

03:30.000 --> 03:32.950
Mr. Duval is very angry.

03:33.000 --> 03:35.100
No, he says.

03:35.200 --> 03:42.950
The next morning Mr. Duval goes to his boat and sees that it is under the water.

03:43.000 --> 03:48.250
Oh, no, he says. I don't understand.

03:48.400 --> 03:51.500
Hannah comes later that morning.

03:51.600 --> 03:57.600
The radio says there is a strong storm coming, a hurricane.

03:57.800 --> 04:02.600
She wants to help Mr. Duval get his boat into the boat house,

04:02.650 --> 04:07.600
but now she sees the glass bottomed boat under the water.

04:07.700 --> 04:12.400
This is Max Marker's work, says Hannah. 

04:12.500 --> 04:15.300
He wants to destroy your business.

04:15.400 --> 04:19.950
I'm an old man, says Mr. Duval.

04:20.000 --> 04:25.600
I'm too tired to fight Max Marker and his nasty games.

04:25.700 --> 04:28.200
I'm not, says Hannah. 

04:28.300 --> 04:31.950
I'm going to his house to see him.

04:32.000 --> 04:35.950
But it is too late. The hurricane is coming.

04:36.000 --> 04:40.600
We must get to my house, says Mr. Duval.

04:40.800 --> 04:48.500
The hurricane hits the island at 11 o'clock that morning.

04:48.600 --> 04:53.950
It pulls trees from the ground and they crash down on houses.

04:54.000 --> 04:58.950
Cars roll across the road like children's toys.

04:59.000 --> 05:03.950
Soon, many of the island's roads are under water.

05:04.000 --> 05:10.950
The strong wind throws Max Marker's boat out of the water and against a wall.

05:11.000 --> 05:18.100
Hannah and Mr. Duval are safe in a room under the old man's house.

05:20.000 --> 05:24.500
The hurricane goes on for four hours.

05:24.600 --> 05:28.950
Slowly, the wind gets weaker and weaker.

05:29.000 --> 05:33.950
Two hours later, people start to come out of their houses.

05:34.000 --> 05:38.000
The rain stops.

05:39.000 --> 05:44.950
Now I can go to see Max Marker about his nasty games, says Hannah.

05:45.000 --> 05:48.800
What can you do, says Mr. Duval?

05:48.900 --> 05:50.950
How can you stop him?

05:51.000 --> 05:54.850
I don't know, says Hannah angrily.

05:54.900 --> 06:00.000
But I can do something and she runs off.

06:06.000 --> 06:09.500
Hannah goes to Max Marker's big house.

06:10.000 --> 06:12.500
She sees the work of the hurricane.

06:13.000 --> 06:15.950
Some of his house is gone.

06:16.000 --> 06:22.500
Where is Max Marker? She thinks. Is he inside?
 
06:23.000 --> 06:26.950
She starts to run to the house, but she is afraid.

06:27.000 --> 06:33.950
Max Marker is inside the house and he cannot get out.

06:34.000 --> 06:40.500
Help! Help! He says, I'm going to die!
 
06:40.800 --> 06:46.700
The wind takes his words and carries them away.

06:46.800 --> 06:51.950
Hannah can hear Max Marker, but she cannot see him.

06:52.000 --> 06:56.100
Where are you? She says, here!  

06:56.200 --> 06:59.950
He says, I'm over here!

07:00.000 --> 07:02.950
Suddenly, she sees him.

07:03.000 --> 07:06.950
He's not laughing now, she thinks.

07:07.000 --> 07:11.950
There are stones and some of the roof on top of him.

07:12.000 --> 07:17.950
Help me! He cries. Please! I'm coming!
 
07:18.000 --> 07:30.500
She tells him, Hannah climbs across and starts to pull the stones off him.

07:30.600 --> 07:35.200
It is not easy. The stones are very heavy.

07:35.300 --> 07:40.800
She gets one off him.

07:41.000 --> 07:42.600
Then the next one.

07:42.700 --> 07:50.100
Faster! He tells her, work faster!

07:50.200 --> 07:54.400
I can't! She cries.

07:54.500 --> 07:58.400
Suddenly, there is a noise above her.

07:58.800 --> 08:03.950
Hannah looks up. Some of the roof is coming down.

08:04.000 --> 08:11.950
Help! Says Max, and he starts to cry.
  
08:12.000 --> 08:23.900
Hannah jumps away and the roof crashes down near her.

08:24.100 --> 08:29.500
She waits for ten seconds and she can see again.

08:29.600 --> 08:33.950
She climbs back across the stones to Max Marker.

08:34.000 --> 08:37.300
He is very happy to see her.

08:37.400 --> 08:41.700
How long before all the house comes down?

08:41.900 --> 08:45.950
Things, Hannah. Can I get him out quickly?

08:46.000 --> 08:49.000
She starts to work faster.

08:51.000 --> 08:55.200
Max can move now, but he is very weak.

08:55.300 --> 09:00.500
He stands up slowly. Then he climbs out of the house.

09:00.600 --> 09:04.950
Hannah helps him across the street. They look back.

09:05.000 --> 09:14.300
The house crashes to the ground.

09:14.400 --> 09:17.950
But Max Marker is smiling now.

09:18.000 --> 09:19.950
You're very brave.

09:20.000 --> 09:23.950
He says, thank you, my friend.

09:24.000 --> 09:28.950
I'm not your friend, says Hannah.

09:29.000 --> 09:33.500
How can I pay you? Says Max.
 
09:33.600 --> 09:40.500
Pay for Mr. Duval's boat, says Hannah, and stop your nasty games.

09:40.600 --> 09:45.400
Work together with the two boats. Don't fight.

09:45.500 --> 09:48.950
Okay, says Max Marker.

09:49.000 --> 09:51.950
But what can I give you?

09:52.000 --> 09:55.950
I don't want anything, says Hannah.

09:56.000 --> 10:00.400
Some money, asks Max.

10:00.500 --> 10:03.350
No thank you, says Hannah.

10:03.500 --> 10:05.950
Money isn't everything.

10:06.000 --> 10:07.950
Yes.

10:08.000 --> 10:13.000
I'm starting to understand that, says Max.

10:22.000 --> 10:51.000
(Thank you)
 
